    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.algebraic_connectivity - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.algebraic_connectivity.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.algebraic_connectivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the algebraic connectivity of an undirected graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.algebraic_connectivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the algebraic connectivity of an undirected graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.algebraic_connectivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get the algebraic connectivity of an undirected graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet the algebraic connectivity of an undirected graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L90656-L90753){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.algebraic_connectivity(\n    normalized=False,\n    weighted=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Algebraic connectivity](../assets/graphs/algebraic-connectivity.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left, a six-node cycle whose closing edge F–A is in the accent color; right, the same nodes without that edge (dashed), a path. The cycle's algebraic connectivity is 1.0 and the path's only 0.268: the path is much easier to cut in two.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe algebraic connectivity (Fiedler, 1973) is the second smallest eigenvalue of the\nLaplacian. It is `0` exactly when the graph is disconnected, and grows the harder the\ngraph is to cut apart: without weights or normalization, it is at most the node\nconnectivity of any graph that isn't complete, and so at most the edge connectivity. It\nalso controls how fast random walks mix, synchronization spreads, and consensus is\nreached. Bottleneck graphs (two clusters joined by a thin link, long paths) have small\nvalues; expanders and dense graphs have large ones. The matching eigenvector is\n`fiedler_vector()`.\n\nLarge graphs use a sparse eigensolver, so this scales to big networks. Matches NetworkX's\n`algebraic_connectivity()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, use the normalized Laplacian (see `normalized_laplacian_matrix()`).\n    Default is `False`.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph. Weights must be\n    non-negative.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The algebraic connectivity (`0.0` for a disconnected graph).\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed, has fewer than two nodes, or has a negative weight.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~fiedler_vector`) \n\n:   The eigenvector that goes with this eigenvalue.\n\n[](`~laplacian_spectrum`) \n\n:   All the smallest eigenvalues, not just the second.\n\n[](`~edge_connectivity`) \n\n:   The fewest edges whose removal disconnects the graph.\n\n[](`~kemeny_constant`) \n\n:   Another spectral measure of how well connected a graph is.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nClosing a path into a cycle makes it harder to cut apart, and the algebraic connectivity\ngrows:\n\n::: {#d6975c16 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\ncycle = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"A\")]\n)\n\nround(path.algebraic_connectivity(), 3), cycle.algebraic_connectivity()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(0.586, 2.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### One more friendship\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Only five friendships cross between the clubs, so the algebraic\nconnectivity is low. A new friendship between Femi and Sven, at the two ends of\n`spectral_ordering()`, raises it the most of any one friendship; a new one within the\nchess club, between Femi and Ada, hardly changes it:\n\n::: {#80aa9a4e .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ndef connectivity(graph):\n    return round(graph.algebraic_connectivity(), 3)\n\n(\n    connectivity(ec.friends()),\n    connectivity(ec.friends().add_edge(\"Femi\", \"Sven\")),\n    connectivity(ec.friends().add_edge(\"Femi\", \"Ada\")),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(0.212, 0.377, 0.213)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#724dc902 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.friends().add_edge(\"Femi\", \"Sven\").plot(\n    highlight=[(\"Femi\", \"Sven\")], color_by=\"club\",\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=8,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</